    description: "From the WI-kosup knob census (2026-10-28; /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/kosup_reader_census_10282026/C_knobs.md K2). An io_primitives OVERLAY's stdlib_other: section is honoured, though the loader strips stdlib_modules / stdlib_prefixes from overlays on purpose (load_overlay_catalog's docstring). stdlib_other names stdlib symbols known NOT to be I/O, and _external_potential chain synthesis (io_boundary.py ~:4230) skips anything in it -- so an overlay can mark requests.post as stdlib non-I/O and hide its external_potential chain (reproduced by the census agent; orchestrator confirmed the code path in the pinned tree). If a COMMUNITY overlay can do this, it makes the output cleaner, which ADR-0061 ruling 2 forbids. NOT DETERMINED: whether this can move a verify-claims verdict toward clean. Measure first: a community overlay declaring stdlib_other for a third-party callee, verify-claims before/after."  # 2fd7
